rafasaurus's dotfiles
---------------------

Uses GNU Stow: https://www.gnu.org/software/stow/

Supported on Arch Linux. Install GNU Stow before continuing. Some targets also
require `sudo`, `pacman`, `paru`, Docker, and the repository submodules.

Usage:
```
cd ~
git clone https://github.com/rafasaurus/dotfiles --recursive
cd dotfiles
make stow
```

`make stow` applies the `common` package and, when present, the package named
by `hostname` (for example, `x220`).

Use `make help` to list available targets. `install-udev` writes privileged
system rules and `uninstall-udev` removes all local udev rules. Review those
targets before running them. `make stow` may replace an existing
`~/.config/mimeapps.list`.

Text login (greetd + tuigreet):
```
make install-login
# Save your work, then reboot:
systemctl reboot
```

Disable any other display manager first. Use the tty1 login instead of startw;
dwl exits or crashes return to authentication. Log out of other TTY shells.
Logs: `journalctl -t dwl -b`. Recovery: Ctrl+Alt+F2, log in, run
`sudo systemctl disable greetd`, then reboot.
